---
pagination: { data: languages, size: 1, alias: lang }
permalink: "{{ '/' if lang == 'en' else '/es/' }}bulletin/index.html"
layout: layouts/base.njk
pageKey: bulletin
titleKey: nav.bulletin
descKey: committee.ann.meta_desc
pageScripts: ["/assets/js/committee.js"]
---
{#- The committee's bulletin (/bulletin/; it was /announcements/ — announcements-redirect.njk keeps that
    address working): Google Docs in the Drive "bulletin" folder or content/bulletin/*.md (the data
    keeps its old name: db.announcements, kind "announcement"). Pinned first, full body,
    auto-translated, each with a deep-link anchor (#ann-… or the file's name) and share buttons.
    Below the shared page hero and the committee sub-nav: the posts, one per row at every width (each
    has the page's whole width — two side by side left a long post half as wide, without "In this
    post", beside an empty column); with none, one solid card written for visitors. Then, collapsed,
    "For committee members · Post to the bulletin" (ui.memberHelp, #how-to-post). The ways to keep up
    (digest, RSS, calendar) are in the footer.
    A post's text is whatever Markdown the chair wrote (scripts/sync/announcements.py tidies it):
    `md({ h: 3, ids })` makes its "# …" headings h3 and down, under the post's own h2 title, each with
    an id of its own (#<anchor>--<words>), and .cm-md (committee.css) styles all of it — tables in their
    own sideways-scrolling box, quotes, code, pictures, long addresses that wrap.
    After the text, the post's aside: "In this post" (its sections, when it has two or more: mdToc) and
    its actions. A card with the width for it (every post from 1024px) shows the aside beside the text,
    the two centred as one block and the aside sticky ("In this post" marks the section being read:
    committee.js annToc); a narrower card (phones, tablets, larger text on a laptop) shows only the
    actions, as a bar under the text — committee.css, "the bulletin".
    The hero's right-hand card (the shared hero aside, "Coming up"): the next committee meeting and the
    next event, linking to them. With no posts it is the page's first card on smaller screens and at
    larger text too ("below"); with posts it is hidden there (they come first).
    A post with an `expires` day hides itself once that day is over in Central time, between the daily
    builds too (data-gv-expire: fsDayEnd, app.js GV.expire — never while a button in it has keyboard focus;
    committee.js, also loaded here, leaves these attributes alone); when the last one has gone, the
    "nothing posted" card shows instead (data-gv-expire-list → data-gv-expire-empty), and the sub-nav's
    Bulletin count goes down with them (committeeNav: data-gv-expire-count). A post scheduled
    for a later day (`publish:`, Drive "(from …)") is not in the data before its day at all (build_data). -#}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{%- set anns = db.announcements.items | cmAnnouncements -%}
{%- set pageAbs = page.url | siteUrl(site) -%}
{%- set di = db.status | cmDriveInfo(site) -%}

{%- set nm = site | cmNextMeeting(lang) -%}
{%- set ne = (db.events.items | cmEvents(site, lang)) | where("past", false) | whereNot("committee", true) | first -%}
{%- set neKind = (ne | eventTone) if ne else "" -%}
{%- set toneOf = { gv: "gv", lv: "lv", committee: "grape", booth: "lv" } -%}
{% call(slot) ui.pageHero(lang, "nav.bulletin" | t(lang), "committee.ann.hero_sub" | t(lang), "megaphone", "committee.ann.eyebrow" | t(lang), { side: ("hide" if anns | length else "below") }) %}
{%- if slot == "side" %}
  {%- if nm or ne %}
  {% call ui.heroAside("committee.ann.meanwhile" | t(lang), lang, { id: "ann-aside-title", icon: "calendar-days", href: "/events/" | lurl(lang), linkLabel: "committee.ann.all_events" | t(lang) }) %}
  <ul class="hero-aside-links" role="list">
    {%- if nm %}
    <li>{{ ui.heroAsideLink({ href: ("/meetings/" | lurl(lang)) + "#committee-meeting", label: "committee.events.stat_next_meeting" | t(lang), text: (nm.startIso | fmtDate(lang, "short")) + (" · " + nm.timeLabel if nm.timeLabel else ""), icon: "users", tone: "grape" }, lang) }}</li>
    {%- endif %}
    {%- if ne %}
    <li>{{ ui.heroAsideLink({ href: ("/events/" | lurl(lang)) + "#" + ne.anchor, label: ne.title, text: ("committee.ann.next_event" | t(lang)) + " · " + (ne.rangeLabel if ne.multiDay else ((ne.startIso | fmtDate(lang, "short")) + (" · " + ne.timeLabel if ne.timeLabel else ""))), icon: "calendar-days", tone: toneOf[neKind] or "vine" }, lang) }}</li>
    {%- endif %}
  </ul>
  {% endcall %}
  {%- endif %}
{%- else %}
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="btn-light" href="{{ '/digest/' | lurl(lang) }}">{% icon "mail-plus", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.ann.get_digest" | t(lang) }}</a>
  </div>
{%- endif %}
{% endcall %}

{% committeeNav lang, "bulletin", db %}

<section class="container-page section pt-10 sm:pt-12" aria-label="{{ 'nav.bulletin' | t(lang) }}">
  {% if anns | length %}
  <ol class="cm-ann-list" data-gv-expire-list data-gv-expire-empty="#ann-empty">
    {% for a in anns %}
    {%- set title = a | tx("title", lang) -%}
    {%- set body = a | tx("body_md", lang) or (a | tx("summary", lang)) -%}
    {%- set when = a.date or a.first_seen -%}
    {%- set annEnd = (a.extra.expires | fsDayEnd) if (a.extra and a.extra.expires) else "" -%}
    {#- its sections for "In this post" (two or more — eleventy.config.js mdToc): the same options as its text
        below, so each link finds its heading ("#<anchor>--why-it-matters"); the ids take the words of the
        post's own language (idsFrom), so a section's link is the same on the English and the Spanish page -#}
    {%- set original = (a.extra.body_md if a.extra) or a.summary -%}
    {%- set toc = body | mdToc({ h: 3, ids: a._anchor, idsFrom: original }) -%}
    <li class="min-w-0" data-gv-expire-item{% if annEnd %} data-gv-expire="{{ annEnd }}"{% endif %}>
      <article id="{{ a._anchor }}" class="card cm-ann{{ ' is-pinned' if a._pinned }}" aria-labelledby="{{ a._anchor }}-h">
        <div class="cm-ann-main">
          <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-sm">
            {% if a._pinned %}<span class="badge-lv">{% icon "pin", "size-3" %} {{ "committee.ann.pinned" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
            {% if a.is_new %}<span class="badge-new">{{ "common.new" | t(lang) }}</span>{% endif %}
            <p class="meta-row text-muted">
              {%- if when %}<time datetime="{{ when | isoDate }}">{{ when | fmtDate(lang, "long") }}</time>{% endif %}
              {#- a meta-row item keeps the row's size (its "·" and hanging indent are 1.1em of it): the smaller words go inside -#}
              {%- if a.extra and a.extra.expires %}<span><span class="text-xs text-faint">{{ "committee.ann.until" | t(lang, { date: (a.extra.expires | fmtDate(lang, "medium")) }) }}</span></span>{% endif %}
            </p>
          </div>
          {#- a title the translation left as it was (rejected, or the same words) is in the post's own language -#}
          <h2 id="{{ a._anchor }}-h" class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight text-ink sm:text-[1.75rem]"{% if a.lang and a.lang != lang and title == a.title %} lang="{{ a.lang }}"{% endif %}>
            <a href="#{{ a._anchor }}" class="cm-anchor-link hover:text-gv">{{ title }}<span class="cm-hash" aria-hidden="true">#</span></a>
          </h2>
          {#- lang="…" only when the text shown IS the original: not machine-translated, not the committee's own
              summary_es (its sections in "In this post" are in that language too) -#}
          {%- set bodyLang = a.lang if (a.lang and a.lang != lang and not (a | machineFor(lang)) and body == original) else "" %}
          <div class="prose-site cm-md mt-4 max-w-none"{% if bodyLang %} lang="{{ bodyLang }}"{% endif %}>
            {{ body | md({ h: 3, lang: lang, name: title, ids: a._anchor, idsFrom: original }) | safe }}
          </div>
          {% if a | machineFor(lang) %}
          <details class="cm-original mt-5">
            <summary>{% icon "languages", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.ann.show_original" | t(lang) }} <span class="text-faint">· {{ ("lang." + a.lang) | t(lang) }}</span></summary>
            <div class="prose-site cm-md mt-3 text-[0.95rem]" lang="{{ a.lang }}">
              <p class="font-semibold">{{ a.title }}</p>
              {{ original | md({ h: 3, lang: lang, name: a.title + " (" + (("lang." + a.lang) | t(lang)) + ")" }) | safe }}
            </div>
          </details>
          {% endif %}
        </div>
        {#- The post's aside, after its text (the reading and Tab order at every width): "In this post" — its
            sections — and its actions. A narrow card (phones, tablets) shows only the actions, as a bar
            along the bottom of the card; a wide one (every post on a desktop: one per row) puts the aside
            beside the text, sticky while the post scrolls by (committee.css .cm-ann-side). A <div>, not an
            <aside>: inside the page's named section an aside is a landmark within a landmark (axe
            landmark-complementary-is-top-level); the list is a nav named "In this post" + the title. -#}
        <div class="cm-ann-side">
          {%- if toc | length %}
          <nav class="cm-ann-toc" aria-labelledby="{{ a._anchor }}-toc {{ a._anchor }}-h">
            <p id="{{ a._anchor }}-toc" class="cm-ann-toc-h">{% icon "list", "size-4 shrink-0" %}<span>{{ "committee.ann.in_post" | t(lang) }}</span></p>
            <ol class="cm-ann-toc-list" role="list"{% if bodyLang %} lang="{{ bodyLang }}"{% endif %}>
              {%- for s in toc %}
              <li><a href="#{{ s.id }}">{{ s.text }}</a></li>
              {%- endfor %}
            </ol>
          </nav>
          {%- endif %}
          <div class="cm-ann-actions">
            {#- A post whose whole text is shown above and came from a plain-text file on Drive (.md / .txt) needs no
                "Open the document": Drive would only show the same words as raw text. A PDF, a picture, a Google
                Doc or a .docx keeps the button (there the file itself, or its formatting, is the message). -#}
            {%- set plainText = a.source == "drive" and a.extra and a.extra.body_md and (a.extra.file_type == "MD" or a.extra.file_type == "TXT" or a.extra.file_type == "MARKDOWN" or (a.extra.mime or "").startsWith("text/")) -%}
            {%- set more = a.extra.link if (a.extra and a.extra.link) else (a.url if (a.source == "drive" and a.url and not plainText) else "") -%}
            {%- set isDoc = a.source == "drive" and not (a.extra and a.extra.link) -%}
            {%- set moreIcon = "file-text" if isDoc else "arrow-up-right" -%}
            {#- `url:` may name a file saved next to the post (/bulletin/files/…, the same in both languages) -#}
            {% if more %}<a class="btn-primary btn-sm" href="{{ more if more.startsWith('/bulletin/files/') else (more | lurl(lang)) }}"{% if more.startsWith("http") %} target="_blank" rel="noopener"{% endif %}>{% icon moreIcon, "size-4" %} {{ ("committee.ann.open_doc" if isDoc else "committee.ann.more_info") | t(lang) }}</a>{% endif %}
            {{ ui.autoNote(a, lang) }}
            <span class="cm-ann-gap"></span>
            <button type="button" class="btn-ghost btn-sm cm-ann-copy" data-copy="{{ pageAbs }}#{{ a._anchor }}">{% icon "link", "size-4" %} {{ "common.copy_link" | t(lang) }}</button>
            <button type="button" class="btn-secondary btn-sm" data-share="{{ pageAbs }}#{{ a._anchor }}" data-share-title="{{ title }}" data-share-text="{{ (a | tx('summary', lang)) | excerpt(140) }}">{% icon "share-2", "size-4" %} {{ "common.share" | t(lang) }}</button>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ol>
  {% endif %}
  {#- Nothing posted: one solid card for visitors ("Coming up" — the next meeting and event — is the
      hero's right-hand card, the first card under the hero on smaller screens). With posts it waits,
      hidden, for the last of them to expire between two builds (GV.expire). -#}
  <div id="ann-empty" class="cm-ann-empty is-solo"{% if anns | length %} hidden{% endif %}>
    {{ ui.pageEmpty("megaphone", "committee.ann.empty_title" | t(lang), "committee.ann.empty_text" | t(lang), { id: "ann-empty-h" }) }}
  </div>
</section>

{#- ---------- For committee members (collapsed): how to post to the bulletin ---------- -#}
<div class="container-page">
  {% call ui.memberHelp(lang, "committee.ann.how_title" | t(lang), { id: "how-to-post" }) %}
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[minmax(0,1.2fr)_minmax(0,1fr)] lg:gap-10">
    <div>
      <ol class="space-y-4">
        {% for k in ["1", "2", "3", "4"] %}
        <li class="flex gap-3.5">
          <span class="step-num" aria-hidden="true">{{ k }}</span>
          <p class="leading-relaxed text-muted">{{ ("committee.ann.how_" + k) | t(lang, { panel: (di.panel.label if di.panel else "Panel") }) }}</p>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ol>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-2.5">
        {% if di.url %}<a class="btn-primary" href="{{ di.url }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{% icon "folder-open", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.drive.open_folder" | t(lang) }}</a>{% endif %}
        <a class="btn-secondary" href="mailto:{{ site.contact_email }}?subject={{ 'committee.docs.mail_subject' | t(lang) | urlencode }}">{% icon "mail", "size-4" %} {{ "committee.docs.ask_access" | t(lang) }}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="panel-muted">
      <p class="eyebrow">{{ "committee.ann.where" | t(lang) }}</p>
      {% cmDrivePath lang, di, "bulletin", ("committee.ann.example_name" | t(lang)) %}
      {% if not (anns | length) %}{% cmDriveChecked lang, di %}{% endif %}
    </div>
  </div>
  {% endcall %}
</div>
